"""Built-in configuration templates, embedded so they can be re-created.

Why the YAML files are duplicated here
--------------------------------------
`configs/` remains the source of truth and stays fully editable — this module
is the *seed* used when a file is missing, not a second configuration system.

Without it the platform has no self-healing path: a fresh clone, a Docker image
built without `configs/`, or a user who deletes a profile leaves `resolve()`
failing on every training request with nothing in the UI explaining why.
Measured on an empty directory before this existed: zero profiles listed, and
every resolve raised "No configuration file for algorithm".

Seeding is additive and never overwrites: a file that already exists is left
exactly as the user last saved it.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

